IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `or336-nouns`
IMPORT `or336-art336`

-- Tests for Art. 336 OR (layer 1, or336-art336.l4).
--
-- Every expected value below was written down from the German text BEFORE the
-- file was run, one provision at a time, and sits beside its assertion with
-- the words it comes from. A failing assertion is a finding, never an
-- expectation to edit. JUST TRUE = the text's condition is met; JUST FALSE =
-- the text says no in its own words (a failed "wenn", an "es sei denn" that is
-- met, a "während" that is not met); NOTHING = the text's own wording limits
-- the provision and the case falls outside the limit.

§ `Tests for Art 336`

§§ `Fixtures: facts, positional (OF), with the fields in the order of nouns.l4`

-- (1)(a): because of the characteristic | connected with the employment | substantially impairs cooperation
`1a: none` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`1a: ground only` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`1a: ground, connected` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`1a: ground, impairs` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`1a: ground, both` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`1a: no ground but exceptions` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

-- (1)(b): because the right is exercised | breaches a duty | substantially impairs cooperation
`1b: none` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`1b: ground only` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`1b: ground, breach` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`1b: ground, impairs` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`1b: no ground but exceptions` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

-- (1)(c): given to thwart the claims | that was the only purpose
`1c: none` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE
`1c: thwart, only purpose` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE
`1c: thwart, with another purpose` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE
`1c: only purpose without thwarting` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE

-- (1)(d): because the other party asserts claims | in good faith
`1d: none` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE
`1d: asserted in good faith` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE
`1d: asserted, not in good faith` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE
`1d: good faith without asserting` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE

-- (1)(e): military | civil protection | civilian service | because of a legal duty | the duty was assumed voluntarily
`1e: none` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`1e: military service` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`1e: civil protection service` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`1e: civilian service` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`1e: legal duty, not voluntary` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`1e: legal duty, voluntary` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`1e: voluntary flag without a duty` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- (2)(a): belongs | does not belong | lawful union activity
`2a: none` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`2a: belongs` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`2a: does not belong` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`2a: union activity` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- (2)(b): representative in a body of the business | in a body connected with the undertaking | the employer can prove a justified reason
`2b: none` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`2b: representative in the business, no proof` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`2b: representative in the connected body, no proof` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`2b: representative in the business, proof` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`2b: not a representative, proof` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- (2)(c): mass dismissal | there is a representation | the representation was consulted | the employees were consulted
`2c: none` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`2c: mass dismissal, representation, not consulted` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`2c: mass dismissal, representation consulted` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`2c: mass dismissal, representation, only employees consulted` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`2c: mass dismissal, no representation, employees not consulted` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`2c: mass dismissal, no representation, employees consulted` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`2c: mass dismissal, no representation, stray representation flag` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`2c: no mass dismissal, nobody consulted` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

-- (3): the mandate ended because of the transfer | the day the notice was given | the last day the mandate would have lasted
`3: no transfer` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` OF FALSE, Date 1 6 2027, Date 30 6 2027
`3: transfer, day before the last day` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` OF TRUE, Date 29 6 2027, Date 30 6 2027
`3: transfer, on the last day` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` OF TRUE, Date 30 6 2027, Date 30 6 2027
`3: transfer, day after the last day` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` OF TRUE, Date 1 7 2027, Date 30 6 2027

-- A notice: given by | (1)(a) | (1)(b) | (1)(c) | (1)(d) | (1)(e) | (2)(a) | (2)(b) | (2)(c) | (3)
GIVEN who IS A Party
      fa IS AN `Art 336(1)(a) facts`
      fb IS AN `Art 336(1)(b) facts`
      fc IS AN `Art 336(1)(c) facts`
      fd IS AN `Art 336(1)(d) facts`
      fe IS AN `Art 336(1)(e) facts`
      ga IS AN `Art 336(2)(a) facts`
      gb IS AN `Art 336(2)(b) facts`
      gc IS AN `Art 336(2)(c) facts`
      h IS AN `Art 336(3) facts`
GIVETH A `Notice of termination`
`a notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` OF who, fa, fb, fc, fd, fe, ga, gb, gc, h

`notice: no ground, given by the employer` MEANS `a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`
`notice: no ground, given by the employee` MEANS `a notice` Employee `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`

§§ `Art 336(1)(a)`

-- "wegen einer Eigenschaft, die der anderen Partei kraft ihrer Persönlichkeit zusteht": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(a) the notice is abusive` `1a: ground only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not given because of such a characteristic: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(a) the notice is abusive` `1a: none` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "es sei denn, diese Eigenschaft stehe in einem Zusammenhang mit dem Arbeitsverhältnis": the exception is met: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(a) the notice is abusive` `1a: ground, connected` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "oder beeinträchtige wesentlich die Zusammenarbeit im Betrieb": the exception is met: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(a) the notice is abusive` `1a: ground, impairs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(a) the notice is abusive` `1a: ground, both` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the exceptions are no ground of their own: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(a) the notice is abusive` `1a: no ground but exceptions` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 336(1)(b)`

-- "weil die andere Partei ein verfassungsmässiges Recht ausübt": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(b) the notice is abusive` `1b: ground only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(b) the notice is abusive` `1b: none` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "es sei denn, die Rechtsausübung verletze eine Pflicht aus dem Arbeitsverhältnis": the exception is met: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(b) the notice is abusive` `1b: ground, breach` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "oder beeinträchtige wesentlich die Zusammenarbeit im Betrieb": the exception is met: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(b) the notice is abusive` `1b: ground, impairs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(b) the notice is abusive` `1b: no ground but exceptions` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 336(1)(c)`

-- "ausschliesslich um die Entstehung von Ansprüchen der anderen Partei aus dem Arbeitsverhältnis zu vereiteln": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(c) the notice is abusive` `1c: thwart, only purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- another purpose beside the thwarting: not "ausschliesslich": no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(c) the notice is abusive` `1c: thwart, with another purpose` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(c) the notice is abusive` `1c: none` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(c) the notice is abusive` `1c: only purpose without thwarting` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 336(1)(d)`

-- "weil die andere Partei nach Treu und Glauben Ansprüche aus dem Arbeitsverhältnis geltend macht": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(d) the notice is abusive` `1d: asserted in good faith` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- claims asserted, but not nach Treu und Glauben: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(d) the notice is abusive` `1d: asserted, not in good faith` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(d) the notice is abusive` `1d: none` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(d) the notice is abusive` `1d: good faith without asserting` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 336(1)(e)`

-- each of the four alternatives of the limb is enough:
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `1e: military service` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `1e: civil protection service` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `1e: civilian service` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "eine nicht freiwillig übernommene gesetzliche Pflicht": a legal duty not assumed voluntarily: met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `1e: legal duty, not voluntary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a legal duty assumed voluntarily is not "nicht freiwillig übernommen": no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `1e: legal duty, voluntary` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `1e: none` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `1e: voluntary flag without a duty` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 336(1) as a whole`

-- "ist missbräuchlich, wenn eine Partei sie ausspricht: a. ... e.": any one limb is enough.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: ground only` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: ground only` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: thwart, only purpose` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: asserted in good faith` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: military service` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a party's notice is read the same way whichever party gives it (the paragraph says "eine Partei"):
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employee `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: asserted in good faith` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no limb met: no listed ground in paragraph 1.
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` `notice: no ground, given by the employer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(1) a ground in paragraph 1 makes the notice abusive` `notice: no ground, given by the employee` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 336(2)(a)`

-- "weil der Arbeitnehmer einem Arbeitnehmerverband angehört": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(a) the notice is abusive` Employer `2a: belongs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "oder nicht angehört": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(a) the notice is abusive` Employer `2a: does not belong` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "oder weil er eine gewerkschaftliche Tätigkeit rechtmässig ausübt": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(a) the notice is abusive` Employer `2a: union activity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(a) the notice is abusive` Employer `2a: none` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Die Kündigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses durch den Arbeitgeber": a notice given by the employee is outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(a) the notice is abusive` Employee `2a: belongs` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(a) the notice is abusive` Employee `2a: none` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Art 336(2)(b)`

-- "während der Arbeitnehmer gewählter Arbeitnehmervertreter in einer betrieblichen ... Einrichtung ist, und der Arbeitgeber nicht beweisen kann ...": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: representative in the business, no proof` `3: no transfer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "oder in einer dem Unternehmen angeschlossenen Einrichtung": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: representative in the connected body, no proof` `3: no transfer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the employer can prove a justified reason ("begründeter Anlass"): no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: representative in the business, proof` `3: no transfer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an elected representative ("während ... ist" not met): no, with or without proof.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: none` `3: no transfer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: not a representative, proof` `3: no transfer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Art. 336(3): the representative's mandate ended by a transfer; the protection continues while the mandate would have lasted.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: none` `3: transfer, day before the last day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: none` `3: transfer, on the last day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day after the mandate would have ended: the protection has ended: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: none` `3: transfer, day after the last day` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- during the continued protection the employer can still prove a justified reason: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employer `2b: not a representative, proof` `3: transfer, day before the last day` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a notice given by the employee is outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` Employee `2b: representative in the business, no proof` `3: no transfer` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Art 336(2)(c)`

-- "im Rahmen einer Massenentlassung, ohne dass die Arbeitnehmervertretung ... konsultiert worden sind": met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: mass dismissal, representation, not consulted` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the representation was consulted: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: mass dismissal, representation consulted` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- there is a representation, so the consultation of the employees does not stand in for it: met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: mass dismissal, representation, only employees consulted` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "falls es keine solche gibt, die Arbeitnehmer": no representation and the employees not consulted: met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: mass dismissal, no representation, employees not consulted` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no representation and the employees consulted: no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: mass dismissal, no representation, employees consulted` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no representation: the representation flag does not count: met.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: mass dismissal, no representation, stray representation flag` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not "im Rahmen einer Massenentlassung": no.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: no mass dismissal, nobody consulted` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employer `2c: none` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a notice given by the employee is outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` Employee `2c: mass dismissal, representation, not consulted` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Art 336(2) as a whole`

#ASSERT `Art 336(2) a ground in paragraph 2 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: belongs` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(2) a ground in paragraph 2 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: representative in the business, no proof` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(2) a ground in paragraph 2 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: mass dismissal, representation, not consulted` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(2) a ground in paragraph 2 makes the notice abusive` `notice: no ground, given by the employer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a notice given by the employee: the paragraph does not speak.
#ASSERT `Art 336(2) a ground in paragraph 2 makes the notice abusive` `notice: no ground, given by the employee` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 336(2) a ground in paragraph 2 makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employee `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: belongs` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Art 336(3)`

-- "dessen Mandat infolge Übergangs des Arbeitsverhältnisses endet": the mandate did not end by a transfer: the paragraph does not apply.
#ASSERT `Art 336(3) the protection of the employee representative continues` `3: no transfer` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "besteht so lange weiter, als das Mandat gedauert hätte": the day before the last day, and the last day itself.
#ASSERT `Art 336(3) the protection of the employee representative continues` `3: transfer, day before the last day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336(3) the protection of the employee representative continues` `3: transfer, on the last day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day after: the protection has ended.
#ASSERT `Art 336(3) the protection of the employee representative continues` `3: transfer, day after the last day` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 336 as a whole: a ground the Article lists`

-- paragraph 1 ground, notice by either party:
#ASSERT `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employee `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: asserted in good faith` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: ground only` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph 2 ground, notice by the employer ("im Weiteren"):
#ASSERT `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: mass dismissal, representation, not consulted` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a paragraph 2 ground does not make an employee's notice abusive: only paragraph 1 is read, and it is not met.
#ASSERT `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employee `1a: none` `1b: none` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: belongs` `2b: representative in the business, no proof` `2c: mass dismissal, representation, not consulted` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no listed ground, either party:
#ASSERT `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `notice: no ground, given by the employer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `notice: no ground, given by the employee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the exceptions of (1)(a) and (1)(b) are met and nothing else is: no listed ground.
#ASSERT `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` (`a notice` Employer `1a: ground, both` `1b: ground, breach` `1c: none` `1d: none` `1e: none` `2a: none` `2b: none` `2c: none` `3: no transfer`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
